Test drives the machine with any right, or none, so a Test capability narrowed to RIGHT_R still ticks it;
a call goes through only a capability with the rights its operation needs.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call went through a capability without the rights its operation needs

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -1011,7 +1011,7 @@ static int dispatch(struct thread *t, uint32_t op, uint32_t slot, uint32_t *arg)
         err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_halt(op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         break;
     case CAP_TEST:
-        err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_test(op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
+        err = op_test(op, arg);
         break;
     case CAP_FRAME:
         err = op_frame(t, slot, &cap, op, arg);
